          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-15 16:03:16.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 16:19:15.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21328 efalnd: Register the MR over the DMA mapped entries",
        "message": "LU-21328 efalnd: Register the MR over the DMA mapped entries\n\nThe memory registration was given the number of fragments before DMA\nmapping instead of the number of entries the mapping returned, as\nthe API expects and as o2iblnd does.\n\nIn practice this has no effect today. Without an IOMMU, DMA mapping\nnever merges fragments, so both counts are the same. With an IOMMU,\nthe mapping can merge fragments, but it marks every unused entry\nwith an invalid address, and the conversion to pages stops at the\nfirst such entry, so the registration still covers only the mapped\nentries. Other mappings, such as GPU memory, may not mark unused\nentries this way.\n\nRegister only the entries the DMA mapping returned.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nChange-Id: Iee6d244fc2f54bbfe788e0507eda2e434ede3325\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
